From: perf session 2026-09-11
Subject: [PATCH 0020] wasm64: more speculation successors (call return, ldr-pc trampolines), W64_SPEC_N 32

Follow-up to 0019.  60 % of lookup misses found every goto_tb successor
already translated (batches averaged 2.6-3 members).  Two more successor
sources, both speculation hints only:

1. translator_note_succ(): the return address of a direct call — ARM
   trans_BL / trans_BLX_i record pc_next (no-op outside CONFIG_TCG_WASM64;
   tb->w64_succ grows to 3 slots).
2. The firmware's `ldr pc, [pc, #-4]` call thunks: if a TB's last word
   is e51ff004, the literal after it is the target (read through the
   non-faulting probe's host pointer; an odd/Thumb literal is skipped).
3. Default speculation budget 16 -> 32 (a 16/32/64 sweep was inside
   noise; 32 nominally best).

Measured (W64_DEBUG=1, 25 s boot): batches 29.5k -> 11.3k, members per
batch 3.1 -> 12.7, lookup misses 20k -> 8k (translated TBs 91k -> 144k:
more speculative waste, paid back by fewer modules/misses).
idlebench --quick vs the 0019 dist, both orders:
  t0.5G  44.2 -> 40.8 (-8 %) / 42.9 -> 40.8 (-5 %)
  window 26.7 -> 25.3 (-5 %) / 26.7 -> 25.3 (-5 %)
  t0.25G -8 % / -6 %; rss flat.
Gates: op-suite wasm64 1156/1156, lockstep 250e6 clean, Firefox boots to
idle (no console errors), native suite 4/4.

